# draft-load-filter notes. NO BASE_SHA256 here, deliberately: like
# container/patches/boot-timing (and unlike qwen3.8-flash-next/patches/
# ple-ct-ignore) this NEVER replaces an upstream file. draft_load_filter.pth is
# a new file mounted into site-packages; it installs a sys.meta_path hook that
# wraps upstream functions post-import, looked up by name. If upstream renames
# or removes a target the hook no-ops and prints "[draft-load-filter] NOT
# applied ..." -- the load then reads the whole checkpoint, exactly as
# upstream does. Nothing to re-derive on snapshot bumps.
#
# Hook table (module -> attr), confirmed present at vLLM a44d7b5 (2026-09-26):
#   vllm.model_executor.model_loader.weight_utils
#       should_skip_weight   -- bound BY NAME from ep_weight_filter at import;
#                               safetensors_weights_iterator resolves it as a
#                               module global before f.get_tensor() in its
#                               lazy / eager / torchao branches
#   vllm.model_executor.model_loader.default_loader
#       DefaultModelLoader.load_weights(self, model, model_config)
#                            -- consumes get_all_weights() synchronously via
#                               model.load_weights(...)
# Filter table (draft_load_filter.FILTERS, model class -> rule):
#   Qwen4ExpMTP -> fn:_remap_mtp_weight_name (vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/mtp.py);
#                  keep(name) = _remap_mtp_weight_name(name) is not None, i.e.
#                  exactly what Qwen4ExpMTP.load_weights keeps.
#   Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration, Qwen4ExpForCausalLM -> drop:mtp.
#                  (vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py); their load_weights
#                  map any name containing "mtp." to None via WeightsMapper
#                  orig_to_new_substr={"mtp.": None} (checked before any prefix
#                  rewrite), so keep(name) = "mtp." not in name. Applied only
#                  while that literal is in load_weights' source. On a44d7b5
#                  the real composed mapper drops exactly the 3101 "mtp."
#                  names of this checkpoint, nothing else (checked over all
#                  299545 names).
#                  Savings: 2.51 GiB = ~4.7 s with MTP off; ~0-0.5 s with MTP
#                  on, because the target's read of mtp.* (the LAST 2.3 GiB of
#                  its stream, in model-fp8-mtp-ple) had been warming the page
#                  cache for the drafter, which now reads it cold instead.
#
# Drift signals, all printed to the container log:
#   "NOT applied ..."                         a target or the remap fn vanished
#   "filter was active but the weight iterator never consulted
#    should_skip_weight"                      load format / iterator changed:
#                                             nothing skipped, boot is slow again
#   "Qwen4ExpMTP: read N checkpoint tensors, skipped M before reading them"
#                                             working as intended
# Formats the filter cannot help (they ignore should_skip_weight upstream):
# fastsafetensors, instanttensor, enable_multithread_load, *.bin/*.pt. The
# launcher uses the default load format.
#
# Measured on nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 (2026-09-26, headers): the
# drafter keeps 3103 of the checkpoint's tensors = 4.88 GiB of 123.53 GiB
# (mtp.* 2.51 GiB in model-fp8-mtp-ple + shards 9/10, embed_tokens + lm_head
# 2.37 GiB in shard 9). Before: the drafter pass took 171.6 s over NFS.
